%!PS-Adobe-3.0
%%Title: Three Spheres — a specimen for lib/etching.ps
%%BoundingBox: 0 0 400 340
%%EndComments

% Demo for the photo-to-line-etching library (issue #15,
% lib/etching.ps): et-draw reads a JPEG straight off disk (via
% /DCTDecode, no new Rust code — see the library's header comment) and
% hatches it into a line engraving with ordinary moveto/lineto/stroke.
% examples/etching_source.jpg is a synthetic still life (three shaded
% spheres) generated for this demo, not a real photograph. Run from
% the repo root:
%
%   pscat --page 400x340 examples/etching_demo.ps
%
% Or convert any JPEG of your own — no PostScript required:
%
%   ./scripts/photo_etch.sh -o out.png your_photo.jpg

(lib/etching.ps) run

1 1 1 setrgbcolor clippath fill

20 20 translate
<< /Photo (examples/etching_source.jpg)
   /PageWidth 320 /PageHeight 240
>> et-draw

0 0 0.5 0.5 setcmykcolor
1 setlinewidth
newpath 0 0 moveto 320 0 lineto 320 240 lineto 0 240 lineto closepath stroke

0.1 0.1 0.12 setrgbcolor
/Palatino-Italic findfont 12 scalefont setfont
0 -16 moveto (lib/etching.ps -- tone-driven hatching, no edge detection) show

showpage
